[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Mobile app requirements
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirement

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Requirements for the Flutter app in ``mobile_app/``. Verifications live in ``docs/verifications/mobile/``.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Connection and login

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Configurable server
STATEMENT: >>>
The app shall have no built-in server address; the user enters the server URL in the settings.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Every household runs its own server.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Login
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall log in with a household account; the app shall then use the token from REQ-BE-012.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Expired session
STATEMENT: >>>
When the server rejects the token, the app shall tell the user the session has expired and let them log in again.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Agenda

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-010
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Agenda views
STATEMENT: >>>
The app shall show the agenda as a planning list and as day, week and month views.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-011
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Edit agenda
STATEMENT: >>>
Users with agenda manager rights shall be able to create, edit and delete agenda items, including start and end time and repeat options.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-040

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-012
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Per-person visibility and colour
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to choose per person whether their agenda and tasks are shown and in which colour.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Tasks

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-020
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Task views
STATEMENT: >>>
The app shall show tasks in a day view and a week view.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-021
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Complete tasks
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to mark a task occurrence as done.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-032

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-022
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Edit tasks
STATEMENT: >>>
Users with task manager rights shall be able to create, edit and delete tasks with title, description, icon, date and repeat options.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-022
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-031

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Offline use and refresh

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-030
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Read offline
STATEMENT: >>>
Without a connection the app shall show the agenda and tasks from its local cache and show that it is offline.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-031
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Queue changes offline
STATEMENT: >>>
Creating tasks and agenda items and completing tasks without a connection shall be queued and sent to the server when the connection returns.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Editing and deleting existing items needs a connection.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-032
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Automatic refresh
STATEMENT: >>>
While the agenda or tasks screen is open, the app shall refresh its data every minute; the user can also pull to refresh.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: AI buddy

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-050
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: AI buddy tab
STATEMENT: >>>
The bottom navigation shall show a third destination 'AI buddy' next to 'Agenda' and 'Taken' only while the backend reports the AI buddy as configured (REQ-BE-083); otherwise the navigation shows only 'Agenda' and 'Taken'. The app checks this at start-up and with every automatic refresh (REQ-MOB-032). When the AI buddy becomes unavailable while its tab is open, the app switches to 'Agenda'.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-051
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Messenger-style chat
STATEMENT: >>>
The AI buddy tab shall show the conversation like a messenger app: the user's messages as bubbles on the right, the AI buddy's on the left, each with its time, the newest at the bottom, and a text field with a send button at the bottom. On opening, the app loads the conversation from the backend (REQ-BE-087) and scrolls to the newest message.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-050
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-087

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-052
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Typing indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
While the app waits for the AI buddy's answer, it shall show a bubble on the left with animated dots, as messenger apps do when the other side is typing. The send button is disabled until the answer or an error arrives.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-053
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Errors and offline
STATEMENT: >>>
The chat needs a connection. When the phone is offline or the backend returns an error, the app shall show the Dutch error message below the user's message with a 'Opnieuw' button that sends the message again. Chat messages are not queued for later like other changes (REQ-MOB-031).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-054
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Refresh after changes
STATEMENT: >>>
After each answer of the AI buddy, the app shall refresh its agenda and task data, so that changes made by the AI buddy (REQ-BE-089) show in the Agenda and Taken tabs right away.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-050
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-089

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-055
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Clear the conversation
STATEMENT: >>>
The AI buddy tab shall have an action to clear the conversation, after a confirmation. It clears the conversation on the backend for all of the user's devices.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-MOB-051

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: General

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOB-040
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Dutch interface
STATEMENT: >>>
All user-facing text shall be in Dutch, with Dutch date and time formatting.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
